export default {"G000224":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000224</code></p><h3>Big étale site of an algebraic stack</h3><p>Use the category fibred in groupoids over schemes defining the stack. A family covers if its underlying maps of schemes form an étale covering.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06NV\">Stacks 06NV · inherited topologies on fibred categories</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/stacks/#tag-06NV\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0788\">Stacks 0788 · comparison with the lisse-étale site</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/stacks-cohomology/#tag-0788\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000224\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000298":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000298</code></p><h3>Cardinal bound for group-action representatives</h3><p>In the group-action construction the bound is <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_G(\\kappa)=\\kappa^{\\aleph_0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000T\">Stacks 000T · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000T\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000298\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000295":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000295</code></p><h3>Cardinal bound for scheme representatives</h3><p>For a cardinal <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> put <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_{\\rm Sch}(\\kappa)=\\max(\\kappa^{\\aleph_0},\\kappa^+)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, where <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa^+</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is its successor cardinal.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/046U\">Stacks 046U · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-046U\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000295\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000297":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets with a specified group action · construction · <code>G000297</code></p><h3>Cardinal size of a group action</h3><p>For a group <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> acting on a set <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> use <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">size</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{size}_G(S)=\\max(\\aleph_0,|G|,|S|)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000T\">Stacks 000T · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000T\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000297\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000294":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · construction · <code>G000294</code></p><h3>Cardinal size of a scheme</h3><p>For a scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, take the maximum of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\aleph_0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the number of its affine opens, and the supremum of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|\\Gamma(U,\\mathcal O_X)|</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over all its affine opens <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000H\">Stacks 000H · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000H\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000294\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000292":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000292</code></p><h3>Cofinality of an ordinal</h3><p>The least cardinality of a subset <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\subseteq\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> such that for every <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\xi&lt;\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> some <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in A</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> satisfies <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\xi\\le a</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000E\">Stacks 000E · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000E\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000292\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000247":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces · structure · <code>G000247</code></p><h3>Connected component</h3><p>For a topological space, a component is a subset maximal among its nonempty connected subsets under inclusion.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/004S\">Stacks 004S · connected components · Stacks 004S · common source definition · Stacks 004S · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-004S\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000247\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000290":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000290</code></p><h3>Cumulative hierarchy</h3><p>In ZFC set <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0=\\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_{\\alpha+1}=\\mathcal P(V_\\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda=\\bigcup_{\\alpha&lt;\\lambda}V_\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> at each nonzero limit ordinal.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000B\">Stacks 000B · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000B\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000290\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000226":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000226</code></p><h3>Étale topology on relative prisms</h3><p>On the relative prismatic category, use jointly covering families of completely étale maps of prism rings in the opposite direction. Over <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(B,J)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, these come from <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-completely étale maps out of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B/J</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> whose reductions modulo <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> jointly cover the special fibre.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1905.08229#page=37\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Remark 4.5</a> · <a href=\"https://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/scholze/prisms.pdf#page=37\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Construction 4.4</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000226\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000299":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets with a specified group action · construction · <code>G000299</code></p><h3>Group actions in a fixed rank segment</h3><p>For a fixed group <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, take the full subcategory of left <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-sets whose codes are in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000T\">Stacks 000T · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000T\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000299\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000229":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000229</code></p><h3>Morphism of ringed topoi</h3><p>For ringed topoi <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℰ</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\mathcal E,\\mathcal O)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℱ</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\mathcal F,\\mathcal P)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, choose a geometric morphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℰ</mi><mo>→</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:\\mathcal E\\to\\mathcal F</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a morphism of rings <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">♯</mi></msup><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒫</mi><mo>→</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^\\sharp:f^{-1}\\mathcal P\\to\\mathcal O</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. By adjunction the second datum can be specified as <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒫</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal P\\to f_*\\mathcal O</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01D3\">Stacks 01D3 · morphism of ringed topoi · Stacks 01D3 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites-modules/#tag-01D3\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000229\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000227":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000227</code></p><h3>Nisnevich topology on relative prisms</h3><p>On the relative prismatic category, use the completely étale maps of prismatic objects for which the corresponding family modulo <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(p,J)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is Nisnevich. Each point of the reduced-modulo-<span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(p,J)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> target lifts with unchanged residue field.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1905.08229#page=37\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Remark 4.5</a> · <a href=\"https://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/scholze/prisms.pdf#page=37\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Construction 4.4</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000227\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000230":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000230</code></p><h3>Point of a topos</h3><p>A point of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal E</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a geometric morphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Set</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>→</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Set}\\to\\mathcal E</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Pullback along this morphism is the stalk functor at the point.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Y4\">Stacks 00Y4 · point of a topos · Stacks 00Y4 · geometric morphism from sets</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Y4\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000230\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000291":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000291</code></p><h3>Rank of a set</h3><p>The rank of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is the least ordinal <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> with <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in V_{\\alpha+1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000B\">Stacks 000B · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000B\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000291\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000225":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000225</code></p><h3>Relative v-site of a diamond</h3><p>For a fixed diamond Y, take maps to Y from small v-sheaves. A family covers if it is jointly surjective as a family of v-sheaves. Apply the size conventions of Scholze §14.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.07343\">Scholze, Étale cohomology of diamonds, Definition 14.1(iii)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000225\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000293":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000293</code></p><h3>Relativization to a set</h3><p>For a fixed first-order formula <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and set <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, restrict every quantifier recursively to <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> to obtain <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi^M</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000F\">Stacks 000F · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000F\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000293\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000296":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sets and ordinals in ZFC · construction · <code>G000296</code></p><h3>Schemes in a fixed rank segment</h3><p>For an ordinal <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Sch}_\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is the full subcategory of schemes whose set-theoretic codes are elements of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Membership depends on the code. Existence of an isomorphic representative is invariant under isomorphism.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000H\">Stacks 000H · Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sets/#tag-000H\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000296\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000201":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Local-ring constructions · construction · <code>G000201</code></p><h3>Strict henselization with a specified separable closure</h3><p>For a local ring <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔪</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(R,\\mathfrak m,\\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a chosen separable closure <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa^{\\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the strict henselization is the local map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R\\to R^{\\mathrm{sh}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> constructed in 04GP. Its target is strictly henselian with maximal ideal <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔪</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak mR^{\\mathrm{sh}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and residue field identified with <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa^{\\mathrm{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04GQ\">Stacks 04GQ · Numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 04GQ · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-04GQ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000201\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000228":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000228</code></p><h3>Zariski topology on relative prisms</h3><p>On the relative prismatic category, use the completions of Zariski localizations of prism rings. A family covers when the corresponding opens cover the special fibre, detected on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B/(p,J)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over a prism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(B,J)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1905.08229#page=37\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Remark 4.5</a> · <a href=\"https://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/scholze/prisms.pdf#page=37\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Construction 4.4</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000228\">Open shared record</a></p></article>"};
